OL,3,GNEWSABluetongue restrictions continue
OL,4,Awith disease 'not going away'
OL,5,
OL,6,FRestriction measures put in place in
OL,7,Fsouth-west Scotland in a bid to stop
OL,8,Fthe spread of bluetongue between farms
OL,9,Fare set to continue.
OL,11,FThe Scottish government has announced a
OL,12,Ftemporary control zone covering much of
OL,13,FDumfries and Galloway will join England
OL,14,Fand Wales and become a restricted zone
OL,15,Ffrom Thursday.
OL,17,FUnder the change, livestock such as
OL,18,Fcattle, sheep and other susceptible
OL,19,Fruminants will still need a licence if
OL,20,Fthey are being moved out of the
OL,21,Frestricted zone to the rest of
OL,22,FScotland.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
